2026-10-16T03:04:11.4830217Z   ISSUE_NUMBER: 55928
2026-10-16T03:04:11.4830418Z   ISSUE_TITLE: [BUG]: Vietnamese mistranslations in the app and ui locale dictionaries
2026-10-16T03:04:11.4832259Z   ISSUE_BODY: The Vietnamese app locale has strings that machine translation got wrong, and a few that are inconsistent with the rest of the same dictionary.

Examples:

- `Custom` was `Phong tục` (the word means customs/etiquette)
- `Advanced` was `Trình độ cao` (the phrase means high level)
- `Shell` was `Vỏ bọc` (the word means carapace/shell of a turtle)
- `Subagents` appeared as both `Chất phụ` (secondary matter) and `đại lý phụ` (sub-agency)
- one entry used `tác tử` for agent while the rest of the dictionary uses `tác nhân`
- `Search provider` was `Tìm kiếm nhà cung cấp`, which reads as "search the provider" instead of "provider of search"
- a mistranslation turned the command `opencode pair` into `cặp opencode`
- the timeline preset descriptions referred to a "Used" group that does not exist in the English source

There is also no `vi` glossary, so every translator re-invents the same terms. The repo already documents a per-locale glossary convention in `.opencode/glossary/README.md`.
